Pasi Kallinen <pkalli@cs.joensuu.fi> writes:

> When your character dies in the middle of a multiple-turn [in]action,
> you get "while helpless" appended to the death-reason.
> This patch changes that to be more descriptive, so you can get, eg.
> "while disrobing" or "while sleeping off a magical draught".

Sounds like a good idea. I haven't compiled it in yet, but I suggest
keeping the "helpless" text there for possible third-party utilities that
may look for it and not understand the changed text without it. For
example, the death reasons mentioned as example would be
"while helpless disrobing" and "while helpless sleeping off a magical
draught". Doesn't sound bad to me..
A potential buffer overflow you suspected is that making the killer
string longer may require increasing DTHSZ in topten.c. (IIRC, neglecting
this doesn't actually crash anything, but it may cause the record/logfile
entry to be truncated.)
I haven't checked yet whether the patch actually requires a bigger DTHSZ
with the longest killer descriptions.. 

